-- title:
--   Existence of dual endomorphism data with norm the degree
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero and let $W$ be an affine Weierstrass curve over $F$ that is elliptic, equipped with three pieces of structure: a `GenusOnePlaceGate`, that is a bijection between the group $W(F)$ of points `W.Point` and the set of places of the function field $F(W)$ together with the assertion that every such place has degree $1$; the centredness property `GenusOnePlaceGate.IsCentred`, saying that for each nonsingular affine point $(x,y)$ the images in $F(W)$ of the coordinate-ring classes of $X - x$ and $Y - y$ lie in the nonunits of the valuation subring of the place attached to that point; and `AbelTheorem`, saying that a divisor of degree $0$ on $F(W)$ is principal exactly when the sum of its points in $W(F)$ is $0$. Assume further that for every isogeny endomorphism datum $D$ of $W$ — a structure consisting of an $F$-algebra map $\iota : F(W) \to F(W)$ which is integral as a ring homomorphism, together with the finiteness of $F(W)$ as a module over itself along $\iota$ — the pushforward norm formula holds along $\iota$: for every nonzero $f \in F(W)$, every divisor whose multiplicity at each place $w$ is $\mathrm{ord}_w(f)$, and every place $v$, the pushforward divisor has multiplicity $\mathrm{ord}_v(\mathrm{Norm}(f))$ at $v$. Then for each such datum $D$, writing $\varphi$ for the induced additive endomorphism `D.pointEnd` of $W(F)$ obtained from $\iota$ by pushforward of divisor classes, there exist an additive endomorphism $\hat\varphi$ of $W(F)$ and integers $t$, $n$ with $\varphi + \hat\varphi = t$, $\varphi\hat\varphi = \hat\varphi\varphi = n$ as endomorphisms of $W(F)$, such that $\hat\varphi$ lies in the subring of $\mathrm{End}(W(F))$ generated by the endomorphisms attached to all isogeny endomorphism data, and $n$ equals the $F(W)$-dimension of $F(W)$ taken along $\iota$.
--
--   This is the existence of the dual isogeny in the function-field presentation of endomorphisms of an elliptic curve: $\hat\varphi\varphi = \varphi\hat\varphi = [\deg\varphi]$ and $\varphi + \hat\varphi \in \mathbb{Z}$, with the dual again lying in the subring generated by the endomorphisms coming from isogeny data. It supplies the dual-and-trace input for [`WeierstrassCurve.Affine.IsogenyEndDatum.exists_sq_lt_four_mul_and_forall_exists_finrankAlong_eq`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.Affine.IsogenyEndDatum.exists_sq_lt_four_mul_and_forall_exists_finrankAlong_eq), where the degree form on the endomorphism ring is shown to satisfy the expected quadratic inequality.
